# =============================================================================
# RoofersLabs — PRODUCTION configuration (backend)
# =============================================================================
# This is a map, not a template. There is deliberately no `.env.production` to
# create: production configuration is not a file, and a copy of it on a laptop
# is a leak waiting for a backup, a screen share, or a stolen machine.
#
# Where each value actually comes from
# ------------------------------------
#   Plain values   the ECS task definition, in
#                  infra/terraform/envs/production/main.tf → module "api_service"
#                  → `environment`. Changing one is a Terraform apply.
#
#   Secrets        AWS Secrets Manager, written by
#                  infra/terraform/envs/production/main.tf → module "secrets"
#                  from infra/terraform/envs/production/terraform.tfvars
#                  (gitignored, never committed). ECS injects them into the
#                  container at start; they are never written to disk.
#
#   DATABASE_URL   generated by Terraform from the RDS master password, which no
#                  human ever sees. It exists only in state and in the
#                  `rooferslabs-production/database` secret.
#
# So: to change production configuration, edit Terraform and apply. To read it,
# look at the task definition (plain values) or Secrets Manager (secrets).
# Nothing here should ever be pasted into a shell.
#
#   aws ecs describe-task-definition \
#     --task-definition rooferslabs-production-api \
#     --query 'taskDefinition.containerDefinitions[0].environment'
#
# The variables production sets — for reference only:
#
#   Runtime      NODE_ENV=production  APP_ENV=production  API_PORT
#                API_PUBLIC_URL  WEB_PUBLIC_URL  CORS_ORIGINS  LOG_LEVEL
#   Data         DATABASE_URL (secret)  REDIS_URL
#   Auth         CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY   CLERK_SECRET_KEY (secret)
#                CLERK_WEBHOOK_SECRET (secret, optional)
#   AI           OPENAI_API_KEY (secret)  OPENAI_*_MODEL
#                OPENAI_REALTIME_VOICE (fleet default; a company's own wins)
#   Telephony    TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID (secret)  TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN (secret)
#                TWILIO_MEDIA_STREAM_URL
#   Storage      AWS_REGION  S3_BUCKET_RECORDINGS  S3_BUCKET_UPLOADS
#                SQS_QUEUE_URL  BACKGROUND_JOBS_INLINE
#   Billing      PAYMENTS_ENABLED  PAYMENT_PROVIDER  PADDLE_ENVIRONMENT
#                PADDLE_PRICE_*  BILLING_*
#                PADDLE_API_KEY / PADDLE_CLIENT_TOKEN /
#                PADDLE_WEBHOOK_SECRET (secrets)
#   Push         VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY  VAPID_SUBJECT  VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY (secret)
#
# APP_ENV=production is what makes the API refuse to start against any resource
# named for another environment — see apps/api/src/config/environment-guard.ts.
#
# For local work, use .env.development.example instead.
# =============================================================================
